    "note": "**GATE 4, TAKE 3 — piecewise draw-on, seam-free** (forked from candidate-02: bloom was too chunky; you wanted the pieces back).\n\nThe squares were never the SUBDIVISION — they were the bbox CROPPING. So the pieces are back with nothing to crop: each segment subdivides into a few slivers, and every sliver is a FULL-CELL annular mask. Slivers overlap 2° backward within their segment — same color over same color composites invisibly, so boundaries never show, mid-fade or final. Each piece fades as the eased front reaches its start angle, duration ∝ its arc — the continuous clockwise draw-on.\n\nThe one hard constraint the old crop machinery existed for is handled by BUDGET instead: total slivers ≤ 24 − N − 2 (labels + center reserved), capped 18 — always under the ~25-overlay mask cliff. 3 segments → ~6 pieces each; 8 segments → 1-2 each. Light/static stay one clean mask per segment.\n\nEverything else rides from takes 1-2: content-hug legend + width-caps, equal-band stack, swatch contract, ~90 lines of sliver apparatus still deleted. 54/54 unit (budget + stagger locks), e2e 7/7, battery ×14 canvases ×5 configs incl. 8-seg.\n\nStill open: ship in base? cover/tutorial? legend look-shift? portrait `legend: bottom` now or v3.1?",
